WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.380
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:14.780
The reading from the Sinoxadion for October 18, on which we commemorate the Holy Apostle

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.860
and Evangelist Luke.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:25.140
Saint Luke came from the city of Antioch, probably of a pagan family.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:32.380
From his youth he applied himself to seek after wisdom and to study the arts and sciences.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:39.180
He traveled all over the world to quench his thirst for knowledge and had particular skill

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.340
as a physician and in painting.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:52.660
The gospel he wrote shows his excellent command of Greek, he also knew Hebrew and Aramaic.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:59.460
There is a tradition that Luke was one of the seventy disciples that the Lord Jesus Christ

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:08.540
sent before him, to by two, to announce salvation in the towns and villages.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:15.980
Luke was in Jerusalem at the time of the life-giving passion, and on Easter morning walked with

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:23.500
Klausus towards the village of Emeius, distraught at the loss of the Master.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:30.680
But Satanus was turned into unspeakable joy when Christ, whom they were unable to recognize

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:37.740
when he joined them on the way, revealed to them in the breaking of the bread that he was

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.660
really and truly risen.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:48.180
After the descent of the Holy Spirit on the day of Pentecost, Luke remained for a time

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.660
in Jerusalem, where there were already disciples.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:59.460
Some say that, on his way back to Antioch, he stopped to preach the good news at Sabast

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:06.860
in Samaria, where he obtained the relic of the right hand of the Holy Forerunner that he

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:11.660
took as a precious trophy to his own city.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:18.860
It would therefore be at Antioch that he met St. Paul in the course of his second missionary

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:25.780
journey, and accompanied him thence to proclaim salvation in Greece.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:32.260
But another tradition says that Luke did not know the Lord during his earthly sojourn,

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:39.480
and that he met St. Paul while working as a physician at Thebes in Moetia during the reign

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.240
of Claudius, circa the year 42.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:50.400
The Apostles' fiery words convinced him of the truth that he had vainly sought in the wisdom

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.200
of this world for so many years.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:01.120
Without hesitation he gave up all that he had, and his profession in physical medicine to

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:07.560
follow Paul and become the beloved physician of souls.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:14.400
He went with the Apostle in his journeys from Troas to Philippi, where Paul left him to

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.440
nurture the newly born church.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:24.000
Luke remained in Macedonia for some years, and when Paul visited Philippi again during his

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.880
third journey in the year 58 AD.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:35.560
He sent him to Corinth to receive the collection made by the faithful there for the needs of

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.480
the poor at Jerusalem.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:45.960
They went together to the Holy City strengthening the churches on their way, when Paul was arrested

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:52.080
in Jerusalem, and transferred to Caesarea, Luke remained with him.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:58.120
He accompanied Paul to Rome and describes their difficult and eventful voyage at the end

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.760
of the Acts of the Apostles.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:08.000
Luke wrote his gospel and the Acts of the Apostles at Rome.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.200
In obedience to Paul, dedicating the Acts to Thelfilos, the governor of Achaea who was

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.400
a convert.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:24.200
In his gospel, Luke adds details which are not found in the first two evangelists.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:30.080
In telling the Savior's life, he especially stresses his mercy and compassion for sinful

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.040
humanity, that he has come to visit as a physician.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.920
And in the Acts, after telling of all that happened in the foundation of the church at Jerusalem,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:49.120
he gives most attention to the work of his master St. Paul, who labored more abundantly

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:55.760
than all the other Apostles, in spreading the glad tidings of salvation.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:05:01.200
After two years of imprisonment in Rome, Paul was released and immediately resumed his

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.880
traveling ministry, followed by his faithful disciple, Luke.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:13.500
But Nero launched his furious persecution of the Christians in Rome soon after, and Paul

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:20.560
returned to the city at the risk of his life, to strengthen the faithful there.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:28.120
He was arrested, put in chains, and held in far worse conditions than before.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:35.000
Luke remained steadfastly faithful to his master, while others forsook him.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:41.000
And he was probably present at St. Paul's martyrdom, although he left no written testimony

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.600
to the fact.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:50.520
After the glorious death of the Apostle of the Gentiles, Luke made his way back to Achaea

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.360
preaching the gospel in Italy, Dalmatia, and Macedonia.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:07.320
It is said that, in his old age amid great tribulations, he also evangelized the idolaters in Egypt.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:13.280
He is supposed to have gone as far as the remote the bayed, and to have consecrated St.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.200
Abil, the second bishop of Alexandria.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:25.560
On his return to Greece, Luke became bishop of Thebes in Boetia.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:32.800
He ordained priests and deacons, established churches and healed the sick in soul and body

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.880
by his prayer.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:40.480
The idolaters arrested him there when he was 84 years old.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:46.160
They flayed him alive and crucified him on an olive tree.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:53.120
Many miracles were wrought afterwards by miraculous midon, trickling from his tomb, which was particularly

00:06:53.120 --> 00:07:03.040
effective in the cure of eye diseases for those who, in faith, anointed themselves with it.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:09.400
Many years later, the emperor Constantius, the son of St. Constantine the Great, sent St.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:17.120
Artemios to Thebes to bring the relics of the Apostle Luke to Constantinople, where they

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:23.520
were placed under the altar of the Church of the Holy Apostles with the relics of the Apostles

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.360
Andrew and Timothy.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:32.800
It is the tradition of the Church that St. Luke was the first iconographer and that he painted

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:38.320
an image of the Holy Mother of God in her earthly lifetime.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:45.280
The All Holy Virgin praised his representation and said, May the grace of him, who was born

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:50.480
of me, be upon this image.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:57.240
St. Luke, afterwards painted other images of the All Holy Virgin and of the Apostles, giving

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:04.920
rise in the Church to the devout and holy tradition of veneration of the icons of Christ and his

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.080
saints.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:13.760
For this reason, St. Luke is honored as the patron of iconographers.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:20.720
Through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.880
and save us.
